    "One campaign against the same AugustusV6 runtime at the same address on seven chains (rule 4); this Polygon pull by an MEV bot is the earliest, hours before the first Ethereum one. The callback is compiled into the main runtime, so later diamond cuts never replaced it.",
    "ParaSwap's white-hat rescue (ref tx) pulled approvals through an owner-added diamond facet, not the callback, and is excluded as affiliated. Exploiters who returned funds after negotiation are counted; returns are not subtracted.",
    "Excluded: bot txs moving only a two-unit test token between the bot's own contracts, and pulls of valueless spam tokens. Bridged majors and LSTs without DefiLlama history are priced as the underlying; OPSEC at the WETH the attacker realised; TUNA had no price or proceeds."
